id=a52sxq_tethering_trains
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Tethering train BPF coverage guard
author=CodesRahul96
description=Our BPF loader is frozen: it always loads /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.o, whatever Tethering APEX Google Play has activated, and that APEX's system_server/netd code aborts if a map or program pin its own netd.o defines is missing (crash loop; apexd reverts a fresh update, but a ROM flashed under an already active train has no such safety net). known/ holds the netd.o of the factory Tethering and of every Play train seen in the field (<versionCode>_<label>_netd.o). The build aborts unless a52_netd.o defines every map of each of them with the same definition (ringbuf min_kver lowered to 5.4 by regen.py and 5.10+-only maps excepted) and pins every program they would pin on 5.4.302 at API 37, so a regenerated a52_netd.o can never silently drop a train that phones already run. The other objects the frozen loader takes from the active APEX (offload.o, test.o, clatd.o, dscpPolicy.o; critical, a failed load = reboot,bpfloader-failed loop) are checked too: each known entry needs its <versionCode>_<label>_<obj>.o, and on 5.4.302 at API 37 every map they would create must have a 5.4 map type, every program they would load a 5.4 program type and only 5.4 helpers/instructions, and every pin they define for API 37 must get created unless the factory object does not create it either or known/tolerated.txt lists it. Ships the list as /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.known for k4-mainline-diag. New train: copy its netd.o, offload.o, test.o, clatd.o and dscpPolicy.o (/apex/com.android.tethering/etc/bpf/mainline/, or /cache/k4_mainline/failed_staged_tethering_<obj>.o after a rolled-back update boot) into known/ as <versionCode>_train_<obj>.o, rerun tethering/regen.py --train-progs with its netd.o, rebuild.
